{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01ANNtqXrvnqbiBBP9xzqoia","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have enough context. Let me look at the EXPECTED_STREAM to understand the varint encoding:\n\n```\n0x09, 0x01, 0x42, 0x03, 0x84, 0x05, 0x06, 0x07, 0xc8, 0x09, 0x05, 0x0b, 0x0c, 0x0d, 0x0e, 0x0f\n```\n\nFor write_vint:\n- `0x09` → 1-byte varint (< 64, prefix 00) → `0x09`\n\n\n- `0x01` → 1-byte varint → `0x01`\n- `0x0203` → 2-byte varint (< 16384, prefix 01) → `0x42, 0x03` (0x4000 | 0x0203 = 0x4203)\n- `0x0405_0607` → 4-byte varint (< 2^30, prefix 10) → `0x84, 0x05, 0x06, 0x07` (0x80000000 | 0x0405_0607 = 0x8405_0607)\n- `0x0809_050b_0c0d_0e0f` → 8-byte varint (prefix 11) with the remaining bytes following the pattern\n\nSo the encoding scheme uses a 2-bit prefix to determine the total length: values up to 63 fit in a single byte, up to 16383 need two bytes with a 0x40 prefix, up to about 1 billion need four bytes with a 0x80 prefix, and larger values need eight bytes with a 0xC0 prefix. Now I'm checking what error type variants are defined.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2159,"cache_read_input_tokens":127714,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2159},"output_tokens":11,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0ef721e-e3c5-4ce3-b9f2-772ba297c48d","uuid":"8c5e3bdb-6d25-4998-85a0-112335664224"}
