{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n## 1. Primary Request and Intent\n\nThe user issued a **Phase 4 batch translation task** for the `c2rust` branch of the picoquic project. The goal is to fill in `todo!()` function bodies in 5 Rust files by translating the matching C implementations. Total: **80 `todo!()` bodies** across:\n\n1. `rs/fq/src/lb.rs` — 5 bodies (LB CID encryption)\n2. `rs/fq/src/socks.rs` — 9 bodies (UDP socket abstraction)\n3. `rs/fq/src/cc_common.rs` — 16 bodies (congestion control helpers)\n4. `rs/fq/src/bytestream.rs` — 39 bodies (byte cursor)\n5. `rs/fq/src/config.rs` — 11 bodies (QUIC config)\n\nConstraints: no `unsafe`, no signature changes, no edits outside `rs/fq/src/`, faithful C translation. After all files, run `phase4_check.py`, `cargo fmt`, `cargo test --no-run`, `cargo clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`.\n\n## 2. Key Technical Concepts\n\n- **QUIC varint encoding** (RFC 9000 §16): 1/2/4/8-byte prefix-encoded integers with 2-bit length prefix\n- **ByteStream cursor pattern**: C `bytestream { data*, size, ptr }` → Rust `ByteStream<'a> { data: ByteStreamData<'a>, ptr: usize }` with Borrowed/Owned variants\n- **bytestream_error()** side effect: sets `ptr = size` to make all subsequent ops fail (sticky error)\n- **QUIC LB CID encoding**: three methods (Clear, StreamCipher, BlockCipher) using AES-128-ECB\n- **HyStart / HyStart++**: RTT-rise and loss-based slow-start exit detection\n- **SMOOTHED_LOSS_SCOPE = 32**, **SMOOTHED_LOSS_FACTOR = 1/16**, EMA of drop rate\n- **Arena-based memory model**: C back-pointer `path_x->cnx` eliminated in Rust; `Path` has no back-reference to `Connection`\n- **CongestionNotification enum**: Acknowledgement, Repeat, Timeout, SpuriousRepeat, etc.\n- **PacketContext enum**: Application=0, Handshake=1, Initial=2\n- **`BYTES_FROM_RATE` macro**: `(microseconds * bps) / 1_000_000`\n- **Wire-format family tags**: `WIRE_AF_INET = 2`, `WIRE_AF_INET6 = 10` (Linux canonical values)\n\n## 3. Files and Code Sections\n\n### `xlate/impl_translation_guide.md` (read-only)\nKey translation rules: C `int` 0/-1 → `Result<(), Error>`, `uint8_t*+size` → `&[u8]`/`&mut [u8]`, microsecond time → `crate::Instant`/`Duration`, no `unsafe`.\n\nModule map: `crate::bytestream` ← `bytestream.c`, `crate::socks*` ← `picosocks.c`, `crate::cc_common` ← `cc_common.c`, `crate::config` ← `config.c`, `crate::lb` ← `picoquic_lb.c`.\n\n### `rs/fq/src/bytestream.rs` — **FULLY TRANSLATED**\nAdded private constants and helper methods, then replaced all 39 `todo!()` bodies:\n\n```rust\n// Wire-format constants\nconst WIRE_AF_INET: u64 = 2;\nconst WIRE_AF_INET6: u64 = 10;\n\n// Private helpers added to ByteStream:\nfn data_ref(&self) -> &[u8] { match &self.data { Borrowed(s) => s, Owned(v) => v.as_slice() } }\nfn data_mut(&mut self) -> &mut [u8] { match &mut self.data { Borrowed(s) => s, Owned(v) => v.as_mut_slice() } }\nfn set_error(&mut self) { let cap = self.data_ref().len(); self.ptr = cap; }\n```\n\nKey implementations:\n- `ByteStreamBuf::stream(nb_bytes)`: checks `nb_bytes <= MAX`, returns `ByteStream { Borrowed(&mut buf[..nb_bytes]), ptr: 0 }`\n- `from_slice(bytes)`: `ByteStream { Borrowed(bytes), ptr: 0 }`\n- `as_bytes()` → `&data[..ptr]` (written portion)\n- `tail()` → `&data[ptr..]` (unwritten portion)\n- `capacity()` → `data_ref().len()`\n- `len()` → `self.ptr`\n- `remaining()` → `capacity - ptr`\n- `reset()` → `ptr = 0`\n- `clear()` → `data_mut().fill(0); ptr = 0`\n- `is_finished()` → `ptr >= len`\n- `skip(n)` → advance ptr, set_error on overflow\n- `write_u8/read_u8/peek_u8` — single byte with bounds check\n- `write_u16/read_u16` — `to_be_bytes()`/`from_be_bytes()`\n- `write_u32/read_u32` — same pattern\n- `write_u64/read_u64` — same pattern\n- `write_varint(value)`:\n  ```rust\n  let len = Self::varint_encoded_len(value); // 1/2/4/8\n  match len {\n      1 => d[ptr] = value as u8,\n      2 => { d[ptr] = 0x40 | (value >> 8) as u8; d[ptr+1] = value as u8; }\n      4 => { d[ptr] = 0x80 | (value >> 24) as u8; /* ... */ }\n      _ => { d[ptr] = 0xC0 | (value >> 56) as u8; /* ... */ }\n  }\n  ```\n- `read_varint()`: read first byte, `len = 1 << ((first >> 6) & 3)`, decode accordingly\n- `skip_varint()`: peek first byte, skip `len` bytes\n- `read_vlen()`: read_varint + downcast to usize with overflow check\n- `write_bytes/read_bytes`: bulk copy with `copy_from_slice`\n- `write_cid/read_cid/skip_cid`: `write_u8(id_len)` + raw bytes; read checks `> CONNECTION_ID_MAX_SIZE`\n- `write_str/read_str/skip_str`: varint(len) + bytes; read checks `l > dst.len()`\n- `write_addr/read_addr/skip_addr`: varint(family) + IP octets + u16 port\n- `with_capacity(n)`: `Vec::new()`, `try_reserve_exact`, `resize`, wrap in `Owned`\n- `varint_encoded_len(v)`: `if v <= 0x3F → 1; elif <= 0x3FFF → 2; elif <= 0x3FFF_FFFF → 4; else 8`\n\n### `rs/fq/src/cc_common.rs` — **PARTIALLY TRANSLATED**\n\n`MinMaxRtt::filter_rtt_min_max` — translated:\n```rust\nlet x = self.sample_current;\nself.samples[x] = rtt;\nself.sample_current = x + 1;\nif self.sample_current >= MIN_MAX_RTT_SCOPE { self.is_init = true; self.sample_current = 0; }\nlet x_max = if self.is_init { MIN_MAX_RTT_SCOPE } else { x + 1 };\nself.sample_min = self.samples[0]; self.sample_max = self.samples[0];\nfor i in 1..x_max { /* update min/max */ }\n```\n\n`MinMaxRtt::hystart_loss_test` — EMA smoothed drop rate, returns true when rate > threshold or Timeout.\n\n`MinMaxRtt::hystart_loss_volume_test` — byte-count EMA: `smoothed_bytes_lost_16 -= /16; += nb_lost`; `smoothed_bytes_sent_16 -= /16; += acked + lost`. Returns true for Acknowledgement when rate > SMOOTHED_LOSS_THRESHOLD.\n\n`MinMaxRtt::hystart_test` — RTT rise detection:\n- Guards against `is_one_way_delay_enabled && rtt_measurement == 0`\n- Checks `current_time > last_rtt_sample_time + 1000μs`  \n- Calls `filter_rtt_min_max`, updates `last_rtt_sample_time`\n- Computes `delta_max = max(rtt_filtered_min/4, packet_time_as_duration)`\n- Tracks `nb_rtt_excess`, returns true when excess ≥ MIN_MAX_RTT_SCOPE\n\nStill `todo!()` (design limitations or pending C source reads):\n- `ConnectionCc::sequence_number/ack_number/ack_sent_time` (translatable but not yet done)\n- `PathCc::lowest_not_ack/slow_start_increase/slow_start_increase_ex/slow_start_increase_ex2` — **cannot be faithfully translated** because they access `path_x->cnx->cwin_blocked` and `path_x->cnx->pkt_ctx[app]` via back-pointer, but `Path` in Rust has no back-reference to `Connection`\n- `PathCc::update_target_cwin_estimation/update_cwin_for_long_rtt` (translatable, not yet done)\n- `NewRenoSimState::reset/notify` (C bodies in `newreno.c`, not yet read)\n\n### `rs/fq/src/lb.rs` — **NOT YET EDITED**\n5 bodies to translate from `picoquic/picoquic_lb.c`:\n- `Config::parse` — parses string like `\"<rot><fbel>[cid_len]<C|S[n]|B>-<server_id_hex>[-<key_hex>]\"`\n- `ConnectionIdContext::generate` — dispatches to clear/stream_cipher/block_cipher sub-functions using AES\n- `ConnectionIdContext::verify` — reverses encoding, returns server_id64 or None\n- `Quic::set_lb_cid_config` — validates, creates ConnectionIdContext with AES contexts\n- `Quic::clear_lb_cid_config` — drops AES contexts, clears callback\n\n### `rs/fq/src/socks.rs` — **NOT YET EDITED**\n9 bodies from `picoquic/picosocks.c`:\n- `OsError::is_unreachable` — checks against `[EAFNOSUPPORT, ECONNRESET, EHOSTUNREACH, ENETDOWN, ENETUNREACH]`\n- `ServerSockets::open` — creates IPv6+IPv4 sockets, sets ECN/pktinfo/pmtud options, binds port\n- `ServerSockets::close` — drops each socket slot\n- `ServerSockets::send_through` — dispatches by address family (V4 → index 1, V6 → index 0)\n- `select` — fd_set select loop with timeout\n- `ServerAddress::resolve` — tries inet_pton IPv4/IPv6, falls back to getaddrinfo\n- `parse_cmsg` — parses cmsg ancillary data for pktinfo/TOS/ECN\n- `format_cmsg` — writes IP_PKTINFO/IPV6_PKTINFO/UDP_SEGMENT control messages\n\n### `rs/fq/src/config.rs` — **NOT YET EDITED**\n11 bodies from `picoquic/config.c`:\n- `Config::default()` — sets: `nb_connections=256, connection_id_length=-1, initial_random=3, cwin_max=u64::MAX, idle_timeout=30000, flow_control_max=0, cwin_max=u64::MAX` (rest zeroed/None/false)\n- `Config::set_option` — dispatch table over OptionId variants\n- `Config::command_line` — single-char option dispatch\n- `Config::command_line_ex` — long-form option dispatch\n- `Config::option_letters` — builds getopt string from table\n- `Config::write_usage` — writes help text to `dyn Write`\n- `Config::print_usage` — writes to stderr\n- `Config::set_port` — parses `\"[S]port1[:port2][*threads]\"` format\n- `Config::create_and_configure` — creates Quic context and applies all config options\n\n### C Source Files Read\n- `picoquic/bytestream.c` — complete cursor implementation\n- `picoquic/picosocks.c` — ~1400 lines of socket code (Linux+Windows)\n- `picoquic/cc_common.c` — ~300 lines of congestion helpers\n- `picoquic/config.c` — ~1100 lines of config parsing\n- `picoquic/picoquic_lb.c` — ~515 lines of LB CID encoding\n- `picoquic/cc_common.h` — struct definitions\n\n### Supporting Rust Files Read\n- `rs/fq/src/internal.rs` — `Path` struct (no `cnx` back-pointer), `Connection` struct, `PacketContextState`, `Quic` struct\n- `rs/fq/src/lib.rs` — `Error` enum, `PacketContext` enum, `CongestionNotification`, `PerAckState`\n- `rs/fq/src/tls_api.rs` — `Aes128EcbContext` (Encrypt/Decrypt variants, `new()` and `process()`)\n- `rs/fq/src/utils.rs` — `varint_len(byte0)` implemented, rest `todo!()`\n- `rs/fq/src/tests/bytestream.rs` — test cases verifying exact byte patterns\n\n## 4. Errors and Fixes\n\n- **Write permission rejected**: Attempted to use the `Write` tool to write `bytestream.rs` from scratch, but Write permission was not granted. Fixed by switching to `Edit` tool operati