{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n## 1. Primary Request and Intent\n\nThe session continues a Phase 4 batch translation task on the `c2rust` branch of the picoquic project. The goal is to fill in `todo!()` function bodies in 5 Rust files by translating matching C implementations from `picoquic/`. The files are:\n- `rs/fq/src/cc_common.rs` (partially done in previous session, completing now)\n- `rs/fq/src/config.rs` (11 todo!() bodies)\n- `rs/fq/src/lb.rs` (5 todo!() bodies — not yet started)\n- `rs/fq/src/socks.rs` (9 todo!() bodies — not yet started)\n- `rs/fq/src/bytestream.rs` (fully translated in previous session)\n\nConstraints: no `unsafe`, no signature changes, no edits outside `rs/fq/src/`, faithful C translation. Verification after all files: `phase4_check.py`, `cargo fmt`, `cargo test --no-run`, `cargo clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Key Technical Concepts\n\n- **Rust 2024 edition**: `gen` is a reserved keyword — must use `r#gen` as a variable name\n- **QUIC congestion control**: HyStart, HyStart++, New Reno simulator, embedded in `cc_common.c`/`newreno.c`\n- **Design limitation**: `PathCc::lowest_not_ack`, `slow_start_increase`, etc. need `path_x->cnx` back-pointer not present on Rust `Path` struct; left as `todo!()` with comments\n- **BYTES_FROM_RATE macro**: `(rtt_microseconds * bps) / 1_000_000`\n- **CWIN constants**: `CWIN_INITIAL = 10 * MAX_PACKET_SIZE` = 15,360; `CWIN_MINIMUM = 2 * MAX_PACKET_SIZE` = 3,072\n- **RTT constants**: `TARGET_RENO_RTT = Duration::from_ticks(100_000)`, `TARGET_SATELLITE_RTT = Duration::from_ticks(610_000)`\n- **NewReno simulator**: Two helper functions (`enter_recovery`, `seed_cwin`) are static in C — translated as private methods on `NewRenoSimState`\n- **Option table pattern**: C has a static `option_table[]` mapping enum→letter/name/nb_params/help; replicated in Rust as `static OPTION_TABLE: &[OptionEntry]`\n- **Config defaults** (from `picoquic_config_init`): `nb_connections=256`, `cnx_id_length=-1`, `initial_random=3`, `cwin_max=u64::MAX`, `idle_timeout=30000` (ms)\n- **`set_qlog` vs `set_binlog`/`set_textlog`**: `set_qlog` takes `&(impl AsRef<Path>)`, the others take `Option<&(impl AsRef<Path>)>`\n- **Cipher suite mappings**: `cipher_suite_id=20→CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256`, `128→AES_128_GCM_SHA256`, `256→AES_256_GCM_SHA384`\n- **recovery_start stored as u64**: `NewRenoSimState.recovery_start` is `u64` (not `Instant`), so comparisons use `.ticks()`\n\n---\n\n## 3. Files and Code Sections\n\n### `rs/fq/src/cc_common.rs` — FULLY TRANSLATED\n\n**Import update:**\n```rust\nuse crate::internal::{Connection, Path, CWIN_INITIAL, CWIN_MINIMUM, TARGET_RENO_RTT, TARGET_SATELLITE_RTT};\nuse crate::{CongestionNotification, Duration, Instant, PerAckState};\n```\n\n**ConnectionCc for Connection:**\n```rust\nfn sequence_number(&self, path_x: &Path) -> u64 {\n    if self.is_multipath_enabled {\n        path_x.pkt_ctx.send_sequence\n    } else {\n        self.pkt_ctx[crate::PacketContext::Application as usize].send_sequence\n    }\n}\nfn ack_number(&self, path_x: &Path) -> u64 {\n    if self.is_multipath_enabled {\n        path_x.pkt_ctx.highest_acknowledged\n    } else {\n        self.pkt_ctx[crate::PacketContext::Application as usize].highest_acknowledged\n    }\n}\nfn ack_sent_time(&self, path_x: &Path) -> Instant {\n    if self.is_multipath_enabled {\n        path_x.pkt_ctx.latest_time_acknowledged\n    } else {\n        self.pkt_ctx[crate::PacketContext::Application as usize].latest_time_acknowledged\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**PathCc for Path (design-limited methods left as todo!()):**\n```rust\nfn lowest_not_ack(&self) -> u64 {\n    // DESIGN LIMITATION: C body reads path_x->cnx->is_multipath_enabled and\n    // path_x->cnx->pkt_ctx[app], but Path has no back-pointer to Connection.\n    todo!(\"PathCc::lowest_not_ack requires Connection back-pointer not present on Path\")\n}\n// same pattern for slow_start_increase, slow_start_increase_ex, slow_start_increase_ex2\n```\n\n**PathCc implemented methods:**\n```rust\nfn update_target_cwin_estimation(&self) -> u64 {\n    let max_win = self.smoothed_rtt.ticks() * self.peak_bandwidth_estimate / 1_000_000;\n    let min_win = max_win / 2;\n    if min_win > self.cwin { min_win } else { self.cwin }\n}\n\nfn update_cwin_for_long_rtt(&self) -> u64 {\n    let rtt_cap = if self.rtt_min > TARGET_SATELLITE_RTT {\n        TARGET_SATELLITE_RTT\n    } else {\n        self.rtt_min\n    };\n    let min_cwnd = (CWIN_INITIAL as f64 * rtt_cap.ticks() as f64\n        / TARGET_RENO_RTT.ticks() as f64) as u64;\n    if min_cwnd > self.cwin { min_cwnd } else { self.cwin }\n}\n```\n\n**NewRenoSimState — reset, notify, and private helpers:**\n```rust\npub fn reset(&mut self) {\n    *self = Self::default();\n    self.ssthresh = u64::MAX;\n    self.cwin = CWIN_INITIAL;\n}\n\npub fn notify(&mut self, connection: &Connection, path_x: &Path,\n    notification: CongestionNotification, ack_state: &PerAckState, current_time: Instant) {\n    match notification {\n        CongestionNotification::Acknowledgement => match self.alg_state {\n            NewRenoAlgState::SlowStart => {\n                self.cwin += ack_state.nb_bytes_acknowledged;\n                if self.cwin >= self.ssthresh {\n                    self.alg_state = NewRenoAlgState::CongestionAvoidance;\n                }\n            }\n            NewRenoAlgState::CongestionAvoidance => {\n                let complete_delta = ack_state.nb_bytes_acknowledged\n                    * path_x.send_mtu as u64 + self.residual_ack;\n                self.residual_ack = complete_delta % self.cwin;\n                self.cwin += complete_delta / self.cwin;\n            }\n        },\n        CongestionNotification::EcnEc | CongestionNotification::Repeat\n        | CongestionNotification::Timeout => {\n            if self.recovery_sequence <= ack_state.lost_packet_number {\n                self.enter_recovery(connection, path_x, notification, current_time);\n            }\n        }\n        CongestionNotification::SpuriousRepeat => {\n            if !connection.is_multipath_enabled {\n                if current_time.ticks() - self.recovery_start < path_x.smoothed_rtt.ticks()\n                    && self.recovery_sequence > connection.ack_number(path_x) {\n                    if self.ssthresh != u64::MAX && self.cwin < 2 * self.ssthresh {\n                        self.cwin = 2 * self.ssthresh;\n                        self.alg_state = NewRenoAlgState::CongestionAvoidance;\n                    }\n                }\n            } else if current_time.ticks() - self.recovery_start < path_x.smoothed_rtt.ticks()\n                && self.recovery_start > connection.ack_sent_time(path_x).ticks() {\n                if self.ssthresh != u64::MAX && self.cwin < 2 * self.ssthresh {\n                    self.cwin = 2 * self.ssthresh;\n                    self.alg_state = NewRenoAlgState::CongestionAvoidance;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        CongestionNotification::Reset => { self.reset(); }\n        CongestionNotification::SeedCwin => { self.seed_cwin(ack_state.nb_bytes_acknowledged); }\n        _ => {}\n    }\n}\n\nfn enter_recovery(&mut self, connection: &Connection, path_x: &Path,\n    notification: CongestionNotification, current_time: Instant) {\n    self.ssthresh = self.cwin / 2;\n    if self.ssthresh < CWIN_MINIMUM { self.ssthresh = CWIN_MINIMUM; }\n    if notification == CongestionNotification::Timeout {\n        self.cwin = CWIN_MINIMUM;\n        self.alg_state = NewRenoAlgState::SlowStart;\n    } else {\n        self.cwin = self.ssthresh;\n        self.alg_state = NewRenoAlgState::CongestionAvoidance;\n    }\n    self.recovery_start = current_time.ticks();\n    self.recovery_sequence = connection.sequence_number(path_x);\n    self.residual_ack = 0;\n}\n\nfn seed_cwin(&mut self, seed_cwin: u64) {\n    if self.alg_state == NewRenoAlgState::SlowStart && self.ssthresh == u64::MAX {\n        if seed_cwin > self.cwin {\n            self.cwin = seed_cwin;\n            self.ssthresh = seed_cwin;\n            self.alg_state = NewRenoAlgState::CongestionAvoidance;\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### `rs/fq/src/config.rs` — FULLY TRANSLATED\n\n**Added import:**\n```rust\nuse crate::internal::MICROSEC_HANDSHAKE_MAX;\n```\n\n**Added `OptionEntry` struct and `OPTION_TABLE` static (51 entries):**\n```rust\nstruct OptionEntry {\n    id: OptionId,\n    letter: char,\n    name: &'static str,\n    nb_params: usize,\n    param_sample: &'static str,\n    help: &'static str,\n}\n\nstatic OPTION_TABLE: &[OptionEntry] = &[\n    OptionEntry { id: OptionId::Cert, letter: 'c', name: \"cert\", nb_params: 1, ... },\n    // ... 50 more entries matching C option_table[]\n    OptionEntry { id: OptionId::Help, letter: 'h', name: \"help\", nb_params: 0, ... },\n];\n```\n\n**Helper functions added:**\n```rust\nfn parse_hex_version(s: &str) -> u32 { u32::from_str_radix(s, 16).unwrap_or(0) }\nfn option_entry(id: OptionId) -> Option<&'static OptionEntry> { ... }\nfn option_entry_by_letter(letter: char) -> Option<(usize, &'static OptionEntry)> { ... }\nfn option_entry_by_name(name: &str) -> Option<(usize, &'static OptionEntry)> { ... }\nfn apply_option(config: &mut Config, entry: &OptionEntry, params: &[&str]) -> Result<(), Error> { ... }\nfn collect_params<'a>(entry, p_optind, argv, optarg) -> Result<Vec<&'a str>, Error> { ... }\nfn parse_option_string(opt_string: &str) -> Option<(usize, &'static OptionEntry)> { ... }\n```\n\n**`Config::default()`:**\n```rust\nfn default() -> Self {\n    Config {\n        nb_connections: 256,\n        connection_id_length: -1,\n        initial_random: 3,\n        cwin_max: u64::MAX,\n        idle_timeout: (MICROSEC_HANDSHAKE_MAX.ticks() / 1000) as i32, // = 30000\n        flow_control_max: 0,\n        // all other fields: None / 0 / false / default\n        ...\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**`Config::set_port()` — byte-level parse of `[S]port1[:port2][*threads]`:**\n```rust\npub fn set_port(&mut self, port_string: &str) -> Result<(), Error> {\n    let bytes = port_string.as_bytes();\n    let mut i = 0;\n    // parse optional 'S' prefix\n    // parse p1 digits\n    // parse optional ':' + p2 digits\n    // parse optional '*' + nb_threads digits\n    // validate i == bytes.len() && 0 <= p1,p2 <= 65535\n    self.server_port = p1 as u16;\n    self.local_port = p2 as u16;\n    self.is_port_shared = is_port_shared;\n    self.nb_threads = nb_threads;\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\n**`Config::create_and_configure()` — calls Quic::new and all configuration setters:**\nKey details:\n- `reset_seed = if self.has_reset_seed { self.reset_seed } else { [0u8; 16] }`\n- Passes `None` for `cnx_id_callback` (C also passes NULL here)\n- `_p_simulated_time` parameter ignored (not in Rust `Quic::new` signature)\n- `set_binlog(Some(bin_dir.as_str()))`, `set_textlog(Some(log_file.as_str()))`, but `set_qlog(qlog_dir.as_str())` (no Option)\n- Cipher suite: `match self.cipher_suite_id { 20 => CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256, 128 => AES_128_GCM_SHA256, 256 => AES_256_GCM_SHA384, v => v as u16 }`\n- `ech_create_config_file` is a free function `crate::ech_create_config_file`\n- `EchClient` base64 decode left as `todo!()` since `picoquic_base64_decode` has no Rust equivalent yet\n\n---\n\n### `rs/fq/src/hash.rs` — Pre-existing `gen` keyword fix\n\nRust 2024 reserved `gen` as a keyword. Fixed by renaming `gen` to `r#gen`:\n\n```rust\n// Before:\nlet gen = self.slots[free_idx as usize].generation;\nself.slots[free_idx as usize] = Slot { generation: gen, ... };\n\n// After:\nlet r#gen = self.slots[free_idx as usize].generation;\nself.slots[free_idx as usize] = Slot { generation: r#gen, ... };\n```\n\nApplied with `replace_all: true` for the first occurrence and manually for the `release_slot` function.\n\n---\n\n### `rs/fq/src/splay.rs` — Same `gen` keyword fix (in progress at summary time)\n\nThe same `gen` keyword fix was being applied to `splay.rs` when the summary was requested.\n\n---\n\n### C source files read (read-only reference):\n- `picoquic/cc_common.c` — all CC helper functions\n- `picoquic/newreno.c` — `picoquic_newreno_sim_reset`, `picoquic_newreno_sim_notify`, `picoquic_newreno_sim_enter_recovery`, `picoquic_newreno_sim_seed_cwin`\n- `picoquic/config.c` — full option table, `config_set_option`, `config_set_port`, `picoquic_config_init`, `picoquic_create_and_configure`\n- `picoquic/picoquic_lb.c` — (read in prior session, needed for lb.rs)\n\n---\n\n## 4. Errors and Fixes\n\n1. **`as_slice()` on `&[u8]` (config.rs line 761)**:\n   - Error: `method not found in &[u8]` for `.as_slice()`\n   - Fix: Removed the `.map(|v| v.as_slice())` since `.as_deref()` on `Option<Vec<u8>>` already returns `Option<&[u8]>`\n   - Changed to: `self.ticket_encryption_key.as_deref()`\n\n2. **`set_binlog(bin_dir)` type mismatch**:\n   - Error: expected `Option<&_>`, found `&String`\n   - Fix: `quic.set_binlog(Some(bin_dir.as_str()))`\n\n3. **`set_qlog(qlog_dir)` type mismatch**:\n   - Error: expected `&_`, found `Option<&str>` (signature takes `&_` not `Option<&_>`)\n   - Fix: `quic.set_qlog(qlog_dir.as_str())` (no `Some` wrapper)\n\n4. **`set_textlog(log_file)` type mismatch**:\n   - Error: expected `Option<&_>`, found `&String`\n   - Fix: `quic.set_textlog(Some(log_file.as_str()))`\n\n5. **`gen` reserved keyword (hash.rs, splay.rs)**:\n   - Error: `expected identifier, found reserved keyword 'gen'` in Rust 2024\n   - Fix: Rename `gen` → `r#gen` in both files\n\n---\n\n## 5. Problem Solving\n\n- **Design limitation in PathCc**: `lowest_not_ack`, `slow_start_increase`, `slow_start_increase_ex`, `slow_start_increase_ex2` all need `path_x->cnx` back-pointer which doesn't exist on the Rust `Path` struct. These are left as `todo!()` with explicit design-limitation comments per the instructions (\"if a translation task seems to require a C-side change, surface it instead of making the change\").\n\n- **`p_simulated_time` dropped**: The C `picoquic_create_and_configure` passes `p_simulated_time` to `picoquic_create`, but the Rust `Quic::new` doesn't have this parameter. The Rust `create_and_configure` has `_p_simulated_time: Option<&mut u64>` which is ignored when calling `Quic::new`.\n\n- **`EchClient` base64 decode**: `picoquic_base64_decode` has no Rust equivalent yet, so the EchClient path (non-`\"-\"` value) is left as `todo!()`.\n\n- **`recovery_start` as `u64`**: The `NewRenoSimState.recovery_start` field is `u64`, not `Instant`. Comparisons with `current_time: Instant` use `.ticks()` to convert: `current_time.ticks() - self.recovery_start < path_x.smoothed_rtt.ticks()`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. All User Messages\n\n1. **Session continuation prompt** (from system): This was an auto-generated continuation from a previous session that ran out of context. The summary described what was done previously and asked to continue without acknowledgment.\n\n2. **Summary request**: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\"\n\n---\n\n## 7. Pending Tasks\n\n1. **`rs/fq/src/splay.rs`**: Apply the same `gen` → `r#gen` fix as hash.rs (was in progress when summary requested)\n2. **`rs/fq/src/lb.rs`**: 5 todo!() bodies to translate from `picoquic/picoquic_lb.c`:\n   - `Config::parse` — string format `\"<rot><fbel>[cid_len]<C|S[n]|B>-<server_id_hex>[-<key_hex>]\"`\n   - `ConnectionIdContext::generate` — dispatches to clear/stream_cipher/block_cipher\n   - `ConnectionIdContext::verify` — reverses encoding, returns `Option<u64>`\n   - `Quic::set_lb_cid_config` — validates, creates context with AES\n   - `Quic::clear_lb_cid_config` — drops AES contexts, clears callback\n3. **`rs/fq/src/socks.rs`**: 9 todo!() bodies from `picoquic/picosocks.c` (not yet started)\n4. *