copy the dereferenced `u8` value into `mask[i]`. The mutable borrow is released after the copy completes, so each subsequent iteration can safely access the next element.\n\nActually, I think the simplest approach using `copy_from_slice` is cleaner and avoids any potential borrow checker confusion. I'm defining a function that copies a slice of bytes into the mask array, encrypts it, then XORs the result back into the target region of the original bytes.\n\nSimplifying with slice operations...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1290,"cache_read_input_tokens":124230,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1290},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0ef721e-e3c5-4ce3-b9f2-772ba297c48d","uuid":"3b629981-df53-438a-b7d3-9f5935e242c9"}
