{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\nThis is a continuation of a Phase 4 batch translation session on the `c2rust` branch of picoquic. The goal is to fill in `todo!()` function bodies in Rust source files by translating matching C implementations from `picoquic/`. The files targeted in this session are:\n- `rs/fq/src/splay.rs` — fix the `gen` → `r#gen` keyword issue (Rust 2024)\n- `rs/fq/src/lb.rs` — 5 `todo!()` bodies from `picoquic/picoquic_lb.c`\n- `rs/fq/src/internal.rs` — 2 related stubs (`lb_generate_cid`, `lb_verify_cid`)\n- `rs/fq/src/socks.rs` — 8 `todo!()` bodies from `picoquic/picosocks.c` (partially started)\n\nConstraints from `CLAUDE.md`: no `unsafe`, no signature changes, no edits outside `rs/fq/src/`, faithful C translation.\n\n---\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n\n- **Rust 2024 edition**: `gen` is a reserved keyword — must use `r#gen`\n- **`core::any::Any` downcast pattern**: Store `ConnectionIdContext` as `Box<dyn Any>` in `Quic::connection_id_callback_ctx`, then `take()` + `downcast_mut()` to access it mutably while also passing `&Quic` to avoid borrow conflicts\n- **QUIC Load Balancer CID encoding**: Three methods — Clear (plain copy), StreamCipher (3-pass XOR), BlockCipher (AES-ECB 16-byte block)\n- **`one_pass_stream` algorithm**: Copy nonce bytes into mask, AES-encrypt mask, XOR mask into target\n- **`RotationBits as u8`**: `repr(u8)` enum with values 0-3; `(self.rotation_bits as u8) << 6` for first byte encoding\n- **`server_id_encoded`**: Big-endian encoding of `server_id: u64` padded to `server_id_length` bytes\n- **`Aes128EcbContext`**: Two variants (Encrypt/Decrypt); `new(is_enc, key)` + `process(&mut [u8; 16])` API\n- **Generic `ServerSockets<S: Socket>`**: S has no factory method, making `open()` impossible to implement generically without specialization\n- **`socket2` crate**: Used for UDP socket abstraction (`Socket2Udp` wraps `socket2::Socket`)\n\n---\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n### `rs/fq/src/splay.rs`\n- Fixed two occurrences of `gen` → `r#gen` (Rust 2024 reserved keyword)\n- **In `alloc_slot`** (~line 162):\n  ```rust\n  // Before:\n  let gen = self.slots[free_idx as usize].generation;\n  self.slots[free_idx as usize] = Slot { generation: gen, ... };\n  // After:\n  let r#gen = self.slots[free_idx as usize].generation;\n  self.slots[free_idx as usize] = Slot { generation: r#gen, ... };\n  ```\n- **In `release_slot`** (~line 183):\n  ```rust\n  // Before:\n  let gen = self.slots[idx as usize].generation.wrapping_add(1);\n  Slot { generation: gen, ... }\n  // After:\n  let r#gen = self.slots[idx as usize].generation.wrapping_add(1);\n  Slot { generation: r#gen, ... }\n  ```\n\n### `rs/fq/src/lb.rs`\n- Added private hex parsing helpers:\n  ```rust\n  fn hex_nibble(b: u8) -> Option<u8> {\n      match b {\n          b'0'..=b'9' => Some(b - b'0'),\n          b'a'..=b'f' => Some(b - b'a' + 10),\n          b'A'..=b'F' => Some(b - b'A' + 10),\n          _ => None,\n      }\n  }\n  \n  fn parse_hex_bytes(hex: &[u8], out: &mut [u8]) -> usize {\n      let mut i = 0;\n      let mut written = 0;\n      while i + 1 < hex.len() && written < out.len() {\n          match (hex_nibble(hex[i]), hex_nibble(hex[i + 1])) {\n              (Some(hi), Some(lo)) => { out[written] = (hi << 4) | lo; written += 1; i += 2; }\n              _ => break,\n          }\n      }\n      written\n  }\n  ```\n\n- Updated `use crate::{ConnectionId, Quic, CONNECTION_ID_MAX_SIZE};`\n\n- **`Config::parse`** — parses format `<rot><fbel>[cid_len]<C|S[n]|B>-<server_id_hex>[-<key_hex>]`:\n  ```rust\n  pub fn parse(txt: &str) -> Result<Self, Error> {\n      let bytes = txt.as_bytes();\n      if bytes.len() < 4 { return Err(Error::InvalidArgument); }\n      let mut config = Config::default();\n      // Parse rotation_bits (0-3), first_byte_encodes_length (Y/y/N/n)\n      // Parse optional decimal cid_len\n      // Parse method char (C/c, S/s + optional nonce_len, B/b)\n      // Parse '-' separator\n      // Parse server_id hex (scan to '-' or end, max 8 bytes)\n      // For StreamCipher/BlockCipher: parse '-' + 32-hex-char key\n      // Final: parsed == bytes.len()\n      // Validate cid_len if set\n      Ok(config)\n  }\n  ```\n\n- **`ConnectionIdContext::set_first_byte`** (private):\n  ```rust\n  fn set_first_byte(&self, quic: &Quic, bytes: &mut [u8]) {\n      if self.first_byte_encodes_length {\n          bytes[0] = (self.rotation_bits as u8) << 6 | (quic.local_connection_id_length - 1);\n      } else {\n          bytes[0] &= 0x3F;\n          bytes[0] |= (self.rotation_bits as u8) << 6;\n      }\n  }\n  ```\n\n- **`ConnectionIdContext::one_pass_stream`** (private):\n  ```rust\n  fn one_pass_stream(enc: &Aes128EcbContext, bytes: &mut [u8], nonce_start: usize, nonce_len: usize, target_start: usize, target_len: usize) {\n      let mut mask = [0u8; 16];\n      let copy_len = nonce_len.min(16);\n      for i in 0..copy_len { mask[i] = bytes[nonce_start + i]; }\n      enc.process(&mut mask);\n      for i in 0..target_len { bytes[target_start + i] ^= mask[i]; }\n  }\n  ```\n\n- **`ConnectionIdContext::generate`**:\n  ```rust\n  pub fn generate(&mut self, quic: &Quic, nonce: &ConnectionId) -> ConnectionId {\n      let mut cid = *nonce;\n      {\n          let bytes = cid.as_bytes_mut();\n          self.set_first_byte(quic, bytes);\n          match self.method {\n              Clear => { bytes[1..1+server_id_length].copy_from_slice(&server_id_encoded[..server_id_length]); }\n              StreamCipher => {\n                  let id_offset = 1 + self.nonce_length;\n                  bytes[id_offset..].copy_from_slice(&server_id_encoded[..]);\n                  let enc = self.cid_encryption_context.as_ref().unwrap();\n                  // Three passes (encrypt nonce, encrypt server_id, encrypt nonce again)\n                  Self::one_pass_stream(enc, bytes, 1, self.nonce_length, id_offset, self.server_id_length);\n                  Self::one_pass_stream(enc, bytes, id_offset, self.server_id_length, 1, self.nonce_length);\n                  Self::one_pass_stream(enc, bytes, 1, self.nonce_length, id_offset, self.server_id_length);\n              }\n              BlockCipher => {\n                  bytes[1..1+server_id_length].copy_from_slice(&server_id_encoded[..]);\n                  let enc = self.cid_encryption_context.as_ref().unwrap();\n                  let block = <&mut [u8; 16]>::try_from(&mut bytes[1..17]).unwrap();\n                  enc.process(block);\n              }\n          }\n      }\n      cid\n  }\n  ```\n\n- **`ConnectionIdContext::verify`**:\n  ```rust\n  pub fn verify(&mut self, cnx_id: &ConnectionId) -> Option<u64> {\n      if cnx_id.len() != self.connection_id_length { return None; }\n      let s_id64 = match self.method {\n          Clear => { /* read bytes[1..1+server_id_length] into u64 */ }\n          StreamCipher => {\n              // Copy to local buf, run three decode passes (same as encode), read server_id\n          }\n          BlockCipher => {\n              let mut decoded = [0u8; 16];\n              decoded.copy_from_slice(&bytes[1..17]);\n              let dec = self.cid_decryption_context.as_ref().unwrap();\n              dec.process(&mut decoded);\n              // Read decoded[0..server_id_length] into u64\n          }\n      };\n      Some(s_id64)\n  }\n  ```\n\n- **`Quic::set_lb_cid_config`**:\n  ```rust\n  pub fn set_lb_cid_config(&mut self, lb_config: &Config) -> Result<(), Error> {\n      // Checks: active connections + CID length mismatch → InvalidState\n      // Checks: fn + ctx already set → InvalidState\n      // Checks: CID length > CONNECTION_ID_MAX_SIZE → InvalidArgument\n      // Method-specific validation\n      // Compute big-endian server_id_encoded; check no overflow\n      // Create AES contexts for stream/block cipher\n      // Build ConnectionIdContext\n      self.local_connection_id_length = lb_config.connection_id_length as u8;\n      self.connection_id_callback_ctx = Some(Box::new(context));\n      Ok(())\n  }\n  ```\n\n- **`Quic::clear_lb_cid_config`**:\n  ```rust\n  pub fn clear_lb_cid_config(&mut self) {\n      let is_lb = self.connection_id_callback_ctx.as_ref()\n          .map_or(false, |c| c.is::<ConnectionIdContext>());\n      if is_lb {\n          self.connection_id_callback_ctx = None;\n          self.connection_id_callback_fn = None;\n      }\n  }\n  ```\n\n### `rs/fq/src/internal.rs`\n- Filled in `lb_generate_cid` and `lb_verify_cid` (in the LB CID section at ~line 4210):\n  ```rust\n  pub fn lb_generate_cid(&mut self, nonce: &ConnectionId) -> Option<ConnectionId> {\n      let mut ctx_box = self.connection_id_callback_ctx.take()?;\n      let result = if let Some(ctx) = ctx_box.downcast_mut::<crate::lb::ConnectionIdContext>() {\n          Some(ctx.generate(self, nonce))  // self moved out of ctx_box, so &Quic is fine\n      } else {\n          None\n      };\n      self.connection_id_callback_ctx = Some(ctx_box);\n      result\n  }\n  \n  pub fn lb_verify_cid(&mut self, cid: &ConnectionId) -> Option<u64> {\n      let mut ctx_box = self.connection_id_callback_ctx.take()?;\n      let result = if let Some(ctx) = ctx_box.downcast_mut::<crate::lb::ConnectionIdContext>() {\n          ctx.verify(cid)\n      } else {\n          None\n      };\n      self.connection_id_callback_ctx = Some(ctx_box);\n      result\n  }\n  ```\n  Key trick: `take()` moves ctx_box out of `self.connection_id_callback_ctx`, so `self` can be reborrowed as `&Quic` for `ctx.generate(self, nonce)`.\n\n### `rs/fq/src/socks.rs` (read only, not yet modified)\n- 8 `todo!()` bodies identified:\n  1. `OsError::is_unreachable`\n  2. `ServerSockets::open` (generic design issue — can't create `S` without factory)\n  3. `ServerSockets::close`\n  4. `ServerSockets::send_through`\n  5. `select`\n  6. `ServerAddress::resolve`\n  7. `parse_cmsg`\n  8. `format_cmsg`\n\n### `rs/fq/Cargo.toml` (read only)\n- No `libc` dependency — complicates errno-based `is_unreachable`\n- `socket2 = { version = \"0.5\", features = [\"all\"] }` is available\n\n### `rs/fq/src/tests/picoquic_lb.rs` (read only)\n- Test `cid_for_lb` calls: `set_lb_cid_config`, `lb_generate_cid`, `lb_verify_cid`, `clear_lb_cid_config` in a loop\n- Test `cid_for_lb_cli` calls `Config::parse` against 9 good and 9 bad strings\n- Verified that `CID_FOR_LB_TEST_TXT` strings match the expected `cli_test_configs()` format\n\n### `rs/fq/src/tests/socket.rs` (read only)\n- The `sockets` test calls `ServerSockets::<Socket2Udp>::open(test_port as i32)`\n- It calls `server_sockets.close()`\n- It calls `get_server_address(\"127.0.0.1\", ...)`, `get_server_address(\"::1\", ...)`, `get_server_address(\"localhost\", ...)`\n- `socket_ping_pong` itself is `todo!()`, so the actual UDP send/recv isn't needed yet\n\n### `picoquic/picosocks.c` (read-only C source)\nKey C implementations noted:\n- `picoquic_socket_error_implies_unreachable`: On Unix checks EAFNOSUPPORT, ECONNRESET, EHOSTUNREACH, ENETDOWN, ENETUNREACH\n- `picoquic_open_server_sockets`: Creates sockets[0]=AF_INET6, sockets[1]=AF_INET; sets pkt_info, ECN, binds to port\n- `picoquic_close_server_sockets`: Loops, calls `close()`, sets to INVALID_SOCKET\n- `picoquic_send_through_server_sockets`: index = (AF_INET) ? 1 : 0; delegates to `send_through_socket`\n- `picoquic_get_server_address`: tries `inet_pton` IPv4 then IPv6, else `getaddrinfo` with AF_UNSPEC\n- `picoquic_socks_cmsg_parse`: Iterates cmsgs for IP_PKTINFO/IPV6_PKTINFO (dest addr) and IP_TOS/IPV6_TCLASS (ECN)\n- `picoquic_socks_cmsg_format`: Writes cmsgs for IP_PKTINFO (source addr) and optional UDP_SEGMENT (GSO)\n\n---\n\n4. Errors and Fixes:\n\n- **`gen` reserved keyword in Rust 2024**: `splay.rs` and `hash.rs` both used `gen` as a variable name (reserved in Rust 2024 edition). Fixed by renaming to `r#gen` in both files.\n- **`cargo check` produced only 2 pre-existing warnings** (one in `splay.rs` about `go_left`, one in `config.rs` about unused `Result`). The lb.rs and internal.rs changes compiled cleanly.\n\n---\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n\n- **Borrow checker for `lb_generate_cid`**: The challenge was that `ctx.generate()` needs `&Quic` while `ctx` is borrowed from `self.connection_id_callback_ctx`. Solved by `take()`-ing the ctx_box out of `self` first (making it a local variable), so `self` is free to be reborrowed as `&Quic`.\n- **`one_pass_stream` borrow**: Reads from `bytes[nonce_start..]` and writes to `bytes[target_start..]`. Used per-element copy loop (`for i in 0..copy_len { mask[i] = bytes[nonce_start + i]; }`) to ensure the immutable borrow ends before the mutable write loop starts.\n- **`BlockCipher` block reference**: `<&mut [u8; 16]>::try_from(&mut bytes[1..17]).unwrap()` to get the `&mut [u8; 16]` needed by `enc.process()`.\n- **Generic `ServerSockets::open`**: `S: Socket` has no constructor, so `open` can't be implemented generically. This is a design gap in the stubs. The test uses `Socket2Udp` specifically, but the impl is generic. Will need either a factory trait bound or specialization.\n- **`OsError::is_unreachable` without libc**: No `libc` crate in Cargo.toml. Can use `std::io::Error::from_raw_os_error(self.0).kind()` with `ErrorKind::ConnectionReset | HostUnreachable | NetworkDown | NetworkUnreachable` — covers all cases except `EAFNOSUPPORT`.\n\n---\n\n6. All User Messages:\n\n1. **Session continuation prompt** (auto-generated by system): Continued from a previous context that ran out. The summary described prior work on `cc_common.rs`, `config.rs`, `hash.rs` (gen fix), and that `splay.rs` gen fix was in progress. Instructions to continue without acknowledgment.\n2. **\"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY...\"** — the current summary request.\n\n---\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n\n1. **`rs/fq/src/socks.rs`** — implement