{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BjfZ5p14TeFSGWj6oA2Z5g","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `quic/lb.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Server-side support for the QUIC load-balancer draft\n4\t//! (<https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-quic-load-balancers/>):\n5\t//! parse the LB-supplied configuration string into a [`Config`],\n6\t//! then install a per-server CID-generation / -verification context\n7\t//! ([`ConnectionIdContext`]) on a [`Quic`] via the connection-ID\n8\t//! callback hook.\n9\t//!\n10\t//! ## API shape\n11\t//!\n12\t//! * [`Config::parse`] takes the LB string as `&str` and returns\n13\t//!   the populated config; the C `(char const* txt, size_t\n14\t//!   txt_length)` pair plus zeroed out-parameter collapse to a\n15\t//!   normal Rust constructor.\n16\t//! * [`Quic::set_lb_cid_config`] applies a `Config` to the QUIC\n17\t//!   context, installing the per-server CID context.\n18\t//! * [`Quic::clear_lb_cid_config`] tears the installed context back\n19\t//!   down (no-op when none is installed).\n20\t//! * [`ConnectionIdContext::generate`] / [`ConnectionIdContext::verify`]\n21\t//!   are the per-CID callback bodies.  They are exposed as inherent methods\n22\t//!   so the eventual [`crate::ConnectionIdCallback`] trait impl can\n23\t//!   delegate to them; the C `void* connection_id_cb_data` parameter is\n24\t//!   recovered as `&mut self`.\n25\t//!\n26\t//! ## Field-shape decisions\n27\t//!\n28\t//! * `rotation_bits : 2` — multi-bit C bitfield, kept as `u8`\n29\t//!   (legal range `0..=3`) per the Phase 1 bitfield rule.\n30\t//! * `first_byte_encodes_length : 1` — single-bit C bitfield used\n31\t//!   as a Boolean flag throughout the C body, promoted to `bool`\n32\t//!   (matching the `config.rs` precedent).\n33\t//! * `cid_encryption_context` / `cid_decryption_context` were\n34\t//!   `void*` in C, holding AES-128-ECB contexts produced by\n35\t//!   `aes128_ecb_create` and freed by `aes128_ecb_free` (both\n36\t//!   declared in `tls_api.h`, which has not been translated yet).\n37\t//!   The fields own their contexts in C (the clear path explicitly\n38\t//!   calls the AES destructor), so Rust models them as\n39\t//!   `Option<Box<Aes128EcbContext>>`, with the AES-context type\n40\t//!   forward-declared here as an opaque struct.  `Box::drop` will\n41\t//!   subsume the explicit `aes128_ecb_free` call once Phase 3 gives\n42\t//!   the type a `Drop` impl.\n43\t//! * `server_id: [u8; 16]` and `cid_encryption_key: [u8; 16]` stay\n44\t//!   as fixed-capacity byte arrays — the C declarations are size-16\n45\t//!   arrays and the algorithms are AES-128, so the capacity *is*\n46\t//!   part of the contract.\n47\t\n48\tuse crate::Error;\n49\tuse crate::tls_api::Aes128EcbContext;\n50\tuse crate::{CONNECTION_ID_MAX_SIZE, ConnectionId, Quic};\n51\t\n52\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n53\t// Private hex-parsing helpers.\n54\t\n55\tfn hex_nibble(b: u8) -> Option<u8> {\n56\t    match b {\n57\t        b'0'..=b'9' => Some(b - b'0'),\n58\t        b'a'..=b'f' => Some(b - b'a' + 10),\n59\t        b'A'..=b'F' => Some(b - b'A' + 10),\n60\t        _ => None,\n61\t    }\n62\t}\n63\t\n64\t/// Decode hex bytes from `hex` into `out`, returning bytes written.\n65\t/// C: `picoquic_parse_hexa`.\n66\tfn parse_hex_bytes(hex: &[u8], out: &mut [u8]) -> usize {\n67\t    let mut i = 0;\n68\t    let mut written = 0;\n69\t    while i + 1 < hex.len() && written < out.len() {\n70\t        match (hex_nibble(hex[i]), hex_nibble(hex[i + 1])) {\n71\t            (Some(hi), Some(lo)) => {\n72\t                out[written] = (hi << 4) | lo;\n73\t                written += 1;\n74\t                i += 2;\n75\t            }\n76\t            _ => break,\n77\t        }\n78\t    }\n79\t    written\n80\t}\n81\t\n82\t/// CID-encoding method selected by the load-balancer config.\n83\t/// C: `load_balancer_cid_method_enum`.\n84\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Default)]\n85\tpub enum ConnectionIdMethod {\n86\t    /// Server ID copied in clear after the first byte.\n87\t    /// C: `load_balancer_cid_clear`.\n88\t    #[default]\n89\t    Clear,\n90\t    /// Server ID encrypted with an AES-128-ECB stream cipher keyed\n91\t    /// off a per-CID nonce.\n92\t    /// C: `load_balancer_cid_stream_cipher`.\n93\t    StreamCipher,\n94\t    /// Server ID encrypted with a single AES-128-ECB block.\n95\t    /// C: `load_balancer_cid_block_cipher`.\n96\t    BlockCipher,\n97\t}\n98\t\n99\t/// Number of low bits of the first CID byte that select between\n100\t/// short-lived configurations.  C: `unsigned int rotation_bits : 2`.\n101\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Default)]\n102\t#[repr(u8)]\n103\tpub enum RotationBits {\n104\t    #[default]\n105\t    Zero = 0,\n106\t    One = 1,\n107\t    Two = 2,\n108\t    Three = 3,\n109\t}\n110\t\n111\t/// Configuration parsed from an LB-supplied string and applied to\n112\t/// a [`Quic`] via [`Quic::set_lb_cid_config`].\n113\t/// C: `load_balancer_config_t`.\n114\t///\n115\t/// `repr(C)` is dropped — the struct is purely an internal shape,\n116\t/// never inspected by an LB or another process.\n117\t///\n118\t/// Lives in `crate::lb`; consumers that also import the demo-app\n119\t/// [`crate::config::Config`] should rename one at the import\n120\t/// site (`use crate::lb::Config as LbConfig;`).\n121\t#[derive(Debug, Default)]\n122\tpub struct Config {\n123\t    pub method: ConnectionIdMethod,\n124\t    pub rotation_bits: RotationBits,\n125\t    /// 1-bit field in C; promoted to `bool` to match call-site usage.\n126\t    pub first_byte_encodes_length: bool,\n127\t    pub server_id_length: usize,\n128\t    /// Used in stream-cipher mode.\n129\t    pub nonce_length: usize,\n130\t    pub connection_id_length: usize,\n131\t    pub server_id: u64,\n132\t    pub cid_encryption_key: [u8; 16],\n133\t}\n134\t\n135\timpl Config {\n136\t    /// Parse an LB-format configuration string into a fresh\n137\t    /// [`Config`].  Returns `Err` when the string is malformed,\n138\t    /// the embedded server ID overflows 8 bytes, or the encoded CID\n139\t    /// length is incompatible with the chosen method.\n140\t    /// C: `lb_compat_cid_config_parse`.\n141\t    ///\n142\t    /// The C signature took an out-parameter and a `(char const*\n143\t    /// txt, size_t txt_length)` pair returning an `int`; the Rust\n144\t    /// signature returns the populated struct in the success arm\n145\t    /// and folds the explicit length into the `&str` slice.\n146\t    pub fn parse(txt: &str) -> Result<Self, Error> {\n147\t        let bytes = txt.as_bytes();\n148\t        if bytes.len() < 4 {\n149\t            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n150\t        }\n151\t\n152\t        let mut config = Config::default();\n153\t\n154\t        config.rotation_bits = match bytes[0] {\n155\t            b'0' => RotationBits::Zero,\n156\t            b'1' => RotationBits::One,\n157\t            b'2' => RotationBits::Two,\n158\t            b'3' => RotationBits::Three,\n159\t            _ => return Err(Error::InvalidArgument),\n160\t        };\n161\t\n162\t        config.first_byte_encodes_length = match bytes[1] {\n163\t            b'Y' | b'y' => true,\n164\t            b'N' | b'n' => false,\n165\t            _ => return Err(Error::InvalidArgument),\n166\t        };\n167\t\n168\t        let mut parsed = 2usize;\n169\t\n170\t        // Optional decimal connection_id_length.\n171\t        let mut cid_len: usize = 0;\n172\t        while parsed < bytes.len() && bytes[parsed].is_ascii_digit() {\n173\t            cid_len = cid_len * 10 + (bytes[parsed] - b'0') as usize;\n174\t            parsed += 1;\n175\t            if cid_len >= 256 {\n176\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n177\t            }\n178\t            config.connection_id_length = cid_len;\n179\t        }\n180\t\n181\t        if parsed >= bytes.len() {\n182\t            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n183\t        }\n184\t        let method_char = bytes[parsed];\n185\t        parsed += 1;\n186\t        match method_char {\n187\t            b'c' | b'C' => {\n188\t                config.method = ConnectionIdMethod::Clear;\n189\t            }\n190\t            b's' | b'S' => {\n191\t                config.method = ConnectionIdMethod::StreamCipher;\n192\t                let mut nonce_len: usize = 0;\n193\t                while parsed < bytes.len() && bytes[parsed].is_ascii_digit() {\n194\t                    nonce_len = nonce_len * 10 + (bytes[parsed] - b'0') as usize;\n195\t                    parsed += 1;\n196\t                    if nonce_len >= 256 {\n197\t                        return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n198\t                    }\n199\t                    config.nonce_length = nonce_len;\n200\t                }\n201\t            }\n202\t            b'b' | b'B' => {\n203\t                config.method = ConnectionIdMethod::BlockCipher;\n204\t            }\n205\t            _ => return Err(Error::InvalidArgument),\n206\t        }\n207\t\n208\t        // Hyphen before server ID.\n209\t        if parsed >= bytes.len() || bytes[parsed] != b'-' {\n210\t            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n211\t        }\n212\t        parsed += 1;\n213\t\n214\t        if parsed >= bytes.len() {\n215\t            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n216\t        }\n217\t\n218\t        // Server ID hex (scan to next '-' or end).\n219\t        let hex_len = bytes[parsed..]\n220\t            .iter()\n221\t            .position(|&b| b == b'-')\n222\t            .unwrap_or(bytes.len() - parsed);\n223\t        let hex_end = parsed + hex_len;\n224\t        let mut s_id_bin = [0u8; 8];\n225\t        let s_id_len = parse_hex_bytes(&bytes[parsed..hex_end], &mut s_id_bin);\n226\t        if s_id_len == 0 {\n227\t            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n228\t        }\n229\t        config.server_id_length = s_id_len;\n230\t        for i in 0..s_id_len {\n231\t            config.server_id <<= 8;\n232\t            config.server_id |= s_id_bin[i] as u64;\n233\t        }\n234\t        parsed += 2 * s_id_len;\n235\t\n236\t        // Encryption key for stream/block cipher.\n237\t        if matches!(\n238\t            config.method,\n239\t            ConnectionIdMethod::StreamCipher | ConnectionIdMethod::BlockCipher\n240\t        ) {\n241\t            if parsed >= bytes.len() || bytes[parsed] != b'-' {\n242\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n243\t            }\n244\t            parsed += 1;\n245\t            if bytes.len() < parsed + 32 {\n246\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n247\t            }\n248\t            let key_len = parse_hex_bytes(&bytes[parsed..], &mut config.cid_encryption_key);\n249\t            if key_len != 16 {\n250\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0ef721e-e3c5-4ce3-b9f2-772ba297c48d","uuid":"f5e3c9db-684d-4bec-811f-fadecf4b7073","timestamp":"2026-05-05T16:56:32.896Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/lb.rs","content":"//! Translation of `quic/lb.h`.\n//!\n//! Server-side support for the QUIC load-balancer draft\n//! (<https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-quic-load-balancers/>):\n//! parse the LB-supplied configuration string into a [`Config`],\n//! then install a per-server CID-generation / -verification context\n//! ([`ConnectionIdContext`]) on a [`Quic`] via the connection-ID\n//! callback hook.\n//!\n//! ## API shape\n//!\n//! * [`Config::parse`] takes the LB string as `&str` and returns\n//!   the populated config; the C `(char const* txt, size_t\n//!   txt_length)` pair plus zeroed out-parameter collapse to a\n//!   normal Rust constructor.\n//! * [`Quic::set_lb_cid_config`] applies a `Config` to the QUIC\n//!   context, installing the per-server CID context.\n//! * [`Quic::clear_lb_cid_config`] tears the installed context back\n//!   down (no-op