e issue now — the `generate` case on lines 4216-4220 is explicitly wrapping the result in `Some`, which is the classic `manual_map` pattern that clippy flags. I should replace it with `.map(|ctx| ctx.generate(self, nonce))`. The `verify` case is different though — it returns `Option` directly without wrapping, so that's actually a `manual_and_then` situation.\n\nSince clippy only reported `manual_map` for `lb_generate_cid`, I'll focus on fixing just that one. For the `collapsible_if` lint in config.rs around line 1352, I'm looking at nested conditions where the outer check is `!failed && (self.ech_key_file.is_some() || self.ech_target.is_some())` and the inner one checks if `quic.ech_configure()` fails. These can be combined into a single condition.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1223,"cache_read_input_tokens":103897,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1223},"output_tokens":12,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0ef721e-e3c5-4ce3-b9f2-772ba297c48d","uuid":"c362a53d-75b7-4cb2-9b12-9906bddc32b6"}
